# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 278-285 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, RUN 2, 2026-09-26): the wage withheld — four prohibitions, the
# weaver and the carder, the proselyte and the sojourner, the beast and the vessels (278); the wage's day and night, the ramp, the cry of 15:9 (279); fathers
# and sons — the testimony, the relatives' list (280); the sojourner's judgment — two and three prohibitions, the widow's garment, Martha (281); the harvest —
# robbers and ants, the gentile who converted, the consecrated, the laborers' forgetting (282); THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF — two not three, the buried and the standing,
# the heads of rows, two seahs, the ear and the burden of proof, the lost sela (283 — HEADLESS inside 24:19, read whole from the export); the olives — the early
# ones' generous eye, glory not over the poor, the forgetting and the corner, the analogy of the measure (284); the vineyard — the small clusters, shoulder
# and pendant, the trellis (285). Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(278, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"OPPRESS NOT A HIRELING POOR AND NEEDY" (24:14) — IS NOT "ROB NOT" (LEVITICUS 19:13) ALREADY SAID? WHOEVER WITHHOLDS A HIRELING\'S WAGE TRANSGRESSES FOUR PROHIBITIONS: OPPRESS NOT, ROB NOT, LET NOT THE WAGE STAY OVERNIGHT, AND "ON HIS DAY GIVE HIS WAGE, LET NOT THE SUN SET ON IT". The head row of piska 278 ({SP_(278, 1, "שכל", "הכובש", "שכר", "שכיר")} "whoever withholds a hireling\'s wage"; {SP_(278, 1, "עובר", "משום", "ארבעה", "לאוים")} "transgresses four prohibitions"): THE FOUR SEATS OF ONE WRONG — Leviticus 19:13\'s three and this verse\'s one, the frozen Leviticus cells the callees (the design\'s (a)); "poor and needy" once in the Torah (find 16); the Tosefta\'s row. Fresh.')
srow(278, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'SINCE "TO IT HE LIFTS HIS SOUL" (24:15) — ONLY WORK DONE AT THE RISK OF LIFE? THE WEAVER AND THE CARDER WHENCE? "OPPRESS NOT" — ANY; ONLY THE POOR AND NEEDY? EVERY MAN WHENCE? "OPPRESS NOT" — ANY; WHY "POOR AND NEEDY"? I HASTEN TO EXACT FOR THEM MORE THAN FOR ANY MAN. ({SP_(278, 2, "גרדי", "וסורק", "מנין")} "a weaver and a carder — whence?"; {SP_(278, 2, "מנין", "לרבות", "כל", "אדם")} "whence to include every man?"; {SP_(278, 2, "ממהר", "אני", "ליפרע")} "I hasten to exact"): the work\'s class and the worker\'s class both unbounded — 277:1\'s trope. Fresh.')
srow(278, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF YOUR BROTHERS" — AND NOT OF OTHERS. ({SP_(278, 3, "ולא", "מאחרים")} "and not of others"): the hireling an Israelite. Fresh.')
srow(278, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"OR OF YOUR SOJOURNER" — THE RIGHTEOUS PROSELYTE: FOR HIM ONE TRANSGRESSES TWO PROHIBITIONS; R. YOSE B. R. JUDAH: ONLY "OPPRESS NOT". ({SP_(278, 4, "זה", "גר", "צדק")} "this is the righteous proselyte"; {SP_(278, 4, "שעובר", "עליו", "בשני", "לאוים")} "transgresses two prohibitions for him"; {SP_(278, 4, "משום", "בל", "תעשק")} "on account of \'do not oppress\'"): the proselyte\'s count disputed — Onkelos "your proselyte" (24:14\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(278, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN YOUR GATES" — THE RESIDENT SOJOURNER; ONLY A MAN\'S WAGE? THE HIRE OF A BEAST, OF VESSELS WHENCE? "IN YOUR LAND" — ALL THAT IS IN YOUR LAND. ({SP_(278, 5, "זה", "גר", "תושב")} "this is the resident sojourner"; {SP_(278, 5, "שכר", "בהמה", "שכר", "כלים", "מנין")} "the hire of a beast, the hire of vessels — whence?"): the two sojourners of one verse (14:21\'s lesson); the rent of beasts and tools under the wage\'s clock (Bava Metzia 9:12 the English\'s "cf."). Fresh.')
srow(279, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON HIS DAY GIVE HIS WAGE" (24:15) — THE NIGHT\'S WAGE IS COLLECTED ALL THE DAY, THE DAY\'S WAGE ALL THE NIGHT — WHENCE? LEVITICUS 19:13 "LET NOT THE HIRELING\'S WAGE STAY WITH YOU UNTIL MORNING". The head row of piska 279 ({SP_(279, 1, "ששכר", "לילה", "גובה", "כל", "היום")} "the night\'s wage is collected all the day"; {SP_(279, 1, "ושכר", "יום", "גובה", "כל", "הלילה")} "the day\'s wage all the night"): THE WAGE\'S CLOCK — two windows from two verses (Bava Metzia 9:11 the answer sheet, the English\'s "cf."); the design\'s DV24-04. Fresh.')
srow(279, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"LET NOT THE SUN SET ON IT, FOR HE IS POOR" — EXCLUDING ONE WHO AGREED OTHERWISE WITH HIM. ({SP_(279, 2, "פרט", "לשפסק", "מעמו")} "excluding one who agreed otherwise with him"): the sunset waived by agreement — the clock\'s parameter. Fresh.')
srow(279, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND TO IT HE LIFTS HIS SOUL" — WHY DID HE CLIMB THE RAMP AND HAND YOU HIS LIFE, IF NOT FOR HIS WAGE THAT DAY? WHOEVER WITHHOLDS A HIRELING\'S WAGE, SCRIPTURE COUNTS IT AS IF HE TOOK HIS LIFE. ({SP_(279, 3, "עלה", "זה", "בכבש")} "this one climbed the ramp"; {SP_(279, 3, "כאלו", "הוא", "נוטל", "את", "נפשו")} "as if he took his life"): the wage the life — the effect\'s gravity. Fresh.')
srow(279, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT HE CRY NOT AGAINST YOU TO THE LORD" — A COMMANDMENT NOT TO CRY? 15:9 "AND HE CRIES AGAINST YOU"; A COMMANDMENT TO CRY? "THAT HE CRY NOT"; SIN ONLY IF HE CRIES? "AND IT SHALL BE SIN IN YOU" — EITHER WAY; WHY "AND HE CRIES"? I HASTEN TO EXACT FOR ONE WHO CRIES MORE THAN ONE WHO DOES NOT. READ BEFORE at chapter 15\'s ledger (the needy\'s cry), REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(279, 4, "יכול", "מצוה", "שלא", "לקרות")} "might it be a commandment not to cry?"; {SP_(279, 4, "יכול", "מצוה", "לקרות")} "might it be a commandment to cry?"; {SP_(279, 4, "על", "ידי", "קורא", "יותר", "ממי", "שאינו", "קורא")} "for one who cries more than one who does not cry"): THE TWO CRIES (15:9 and 24:15 — find 7\'s run of six) neither commanded nor forbidden; the sin in you regardless — the same row that closed the release\'s ledger. Reread.')
srow(280, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FATHERS SHALL NOT BE PUT TO DEATH FOR SONS" (24:16) — WHAT DOES IT TEACH, THAT FATHERS DIE NOT FOR SONS\' DEEDS? "EACH FOR HIS OWN SIN" SAYS IT — RATHER, FATHERS NOT BY THE TESTIMONY OF SONS NOR SONS BY THE TESTIMONY OF FATHERS. The head row of piska 280 ({SP_(280, 1, "שלא", "יומתו", "אבות", "בעדות", "בנים")} "fathers not put to death by the testimony of sons"; {SP_(280, 1, "ולא", "בנים", "בעדות", "אבות")} "nor sons by the testimony of fathers"): THE VERSE READ AS A LAW OF WITNESSES, not of guilt — Onkelos writes the same ("by the mouth of sons", 24:16\'s row); 2 Kings 14:6 quotes the verse in its plain sense (find 1 — the pointer OWED, the design\'s (f)). Fresh.')
srow(280, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'WHEN IT SAYS "AND SONS" — TO INCLUDE THE RELATIVES: HIS BROTHER, HIS FATHER\'S BROTHER, HIS MOTHER\'S BROTHER, HIS SISTER\'S HUSBAND, HIS FATHER\'S SISTER\'S HUSBAND, HIS MOTHER\'S SISTER\'S HUSBAND, HIS MOTHER\'S HUSBAND, HIS FATHER-IN-LAW AND HIS BROTHER-IN-LAW. ({SP_(280, 2, "לרבות", "את", "הקרובים")} "to include the relatives"; {SP_(280, 2, "אחיו", "ואחי", "אביו", "ואחי", "אמו")} "his brother, his father\'s brother, his mother\'s brother"; {SP_(280, 2, "וחמיו", "וגיסו")} "his father-in-law and his brother-in-law"): Sanhedrin 3:4 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — THE KINSHIP PARAMETER of the witness (the design\'s DV24-05); 19:15\'s witnesses the callee. Fresh.')
srow(280, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"EACH FOR HIS OWN SIN SHALL DIE" — FATHERS DIE FOR THEIR OWN INIQUITY AND SONS FOR THEIR OWN. ({SP_(280, 3, "אבות", "מתים", "בעון", "עצמם")} "fathers die for their own iniquity"): the verse\'s third clause in its plain sense — Ezekiel 18\'s kin (find 1). Fresh.')
srow(281, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"PERVERT NOT THE JUDGMENT OF THE SOJOURNER" (24:17) — WHAT DO I NEED IT FOR, WHEN 16:19 SAYS "PERVERT NOT JUDGMENT, REGARD NOT PERSONS"? WHOEVER PERVERTS A SOJOURNER\'S JUDGMENT TRANSGRESSES TWO PROHIBITIONS; IF A SOJOURNER-ORPHAN, THREE. The head row of piska 281 — READ BEFORE at chapter 16\'s ledger (the courts\' bribe and perversion), REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(281, 1, "מה", "אני", "צריך")} "what do I need it for?"; {SP_(281, 1, "שכל", "המטה", "דינו", "של", "גר")} "whoever perverts a sojourner\'s judgment"; {SP_(281, 1, "עובר", "בשני", "לאוים")} "transgresses two prohibitions"; {SP_(281, 1, "עובר", "בשלשה", "לאוים")} "transgresses three prohibitions"): 16:19\'S CELL REUSED with a count of prohibitions by the victim\'s class (the design\'s (f)) — the sojourner, the orphan, the sojourner-orphan. Reread.')
srow(281, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND TAKE NOT A WIDOW\'S GARMENT IN PLEDGE" — POOR OR RICH, EVEN MARTHA DAUGHTER OF BOETHUS. ({SP_(281, 2, "בין", "עניה", "בין", "עשירה")} "poor or rich"; {SP_(281, 2, "כמרתא", "בת", "ביתוס")} "as Martha daughter of Boethus"): the widow\'s status alone the bar, her wealth no parameter — Jerusalem\'s richest widow the case. Fresh.')
srow(281, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON: WHAT YOU TAKE IN PLEDGE FROM A MAN YOU DO NOT RETURN TO A WOMAN, LEST YOU GO IN AND OUT AT HER HOUSE AND GIVE HER A BAD NAME. ({SP_(281, 3, "אין", "אתה", "מחזיר", "לאשה")} "you do not return to a woman"; {SP_(281, 3, "להשיאה", "שם", "רע")} "to give her a bad name"): the reason of the bar — the daily return (277:3) would bring the creditor to her door; the chapter\'s one row citing no verse in either file (the ink). Fresh.')
srow(282, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU REAP YOUR HARVEST IN YOUR FIELD" (24:19) — EXCLUDING WHAT ROBBERS REAPED, ANTS GNAWED, THE WIND OR A BEAST BROKE. The head row of piska 282 ({SP_(282, 1, "פרט", "לשקצרוהו", "ליסטים")} "excluding what robbers reaped"; {SP_(282, 1, "וקרסמוהו", "נמלים")} "and ants gnawed"; {SP_(282, 1, "ושברתו", "הרוח", "או", "בהמה")} "and the wind or a beast broke"): the harvest must be the owner\'s act (Peah 2:7 the English\'s "cf."); THE ENGLISH ROW 282:1 CARRIES 282:2\'S TEXT TOO (the gentile who converted, R. Judah\'s sheaf) — the export\'s misplacement, RUN 1\'s 227:11 the precedent. Fresh.')
srow(282, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR HARVEST" — EXCLUDING WHAT GENTILES REAPED; HENCE: A GENTILE WHO REAPED HIS FIELD AND THEN CONVERTED IS EXEMPT FROM GLEANINGS, THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF AND THE CORNER; R. JUDAH OBLIGATES THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF, FOR FORGETTING IS ONLY AT THE SHEAVING. "YOUR HARVEST" — EXCLUDING OTHERS; EXCLUDING THE CONSECRATED: THE SANCTUARY REAPED AND AN ISRAELITE BOUGHT — EXEMPT; A GENTILE REAPED AND AN ISRAELITE BOUGHT — EXEMPT. ({SP_(282, 2, "נכרי", "שקצר", "את", "שדהו", "ואחר", "כך", "נתגיר")} "a gentile who reaped his field and then converted"; {SP_(282, 2, "פטור", "מן", "הלקט", "ומן", "השכחה", "ומן", "הפאה")} "exempt from gleanings, the forgotten sheaf and the corner"; {SP_(282, 2, "שאין", "שכחה", "אלא", "בשעת", "העמור")} "forgetting is only at the sheaving"; {SP_(282, 2, "פרט", "להקדש")} "excluding the consecrated"): Peah 4:6 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — THE CLOCK OF THE DUTY: gleanings and corner at the reaping, the forgotten sheaf at the binding; the design\'s DV24-05 (Leviticus 19:9\'s cells with the sheaf NEW). Fresh.')
srow(282, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: FROM "WHEN YOU REAP YOUR HARVEST … AND FORGET A SHEAF" — WHENEVER HE HAS A HARVEST HE HAS A SHEAF AND A FORGETTING; NO HARVEST, NO SHEAF, NO FORGETTING: THE SANCTUARY REAPED AND AN ISRAELITE BOUGHT — EXEMPT; A GENTILE REAPED — EXEMPT. ({SP_(282, 3, "כל", "זמן", "שיש", "לו", "קציר")} "whenever he has a harvest"; {SP_(282, 3, "יש", "לו", "עמר", "ויש", "לו", "שכחה")} "he has a sheaf and he has a forgetting"; {SP_(282, 3, "קצר", "גוי", "ולקח", "ישראל", "פטורה")} "a gentile reaped and an Israelite bought — exempt"): the same two verdicts by a second route — the sheaf conditioned on the harvest\'s owner. Fresh.')
srow(282, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN YOUR FIELD" — EXCLUDING ONE WHO SHEAVES IN HIS FELLOW\'S FIELD: R. MEIR; THE SAGES OBLIGATE; HENCE: A SHEAF THE LABORERS FORGOT AND THE OWNER NOT, OR THE OWNER FORGOT AND THE LABORERS NOT, OR THE POOR STOOD BEFORE IT, OR THEY COVERED IT WITH STRAW — NOT FORGOTTEN. ({SP_(282, 4, "פרט", "למעמר", "בשדה", "חברו")} "excluding one who sheaves in his fellow\'s field"; {SP_(282, 4, "ששכחוהו", "פועלים", "ולא", "שכחו", "בעל", "הבית")} "which the laborers forgot and the owner did not"; {SP_(282, 4, "עמדו", "העניים", "בפניו")} "the poor stood before it"; {SP_(282, 4, "או", "שחפוהו", "בקש")} "or covered it with straw"; {SP_(282, 4, "אינו", "שכחה")} "is not a forgotten sheaf"): Peah 5:7 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — FORGETTING NEEDS BOTH MINDS, the owner\'s and the laborers\'; the poor\'s own act no forgetting. Fresh.')
srow(283, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND FORGET A SHEAF" — AND NOT THE STACK; EVEN NOT TWO? "FOR THE SOJOURNER, THE ORPHAN AND THE WIDOW LET IT BE"; HENCE: TWO SHEAVES ARE FORGOTTEN, THREE ARE NOT; TWO HEAPS OF OLIVES OR CAROBS, THREE NOT; TWO BERRIES ARE FALLEN GRAPES, THREE NOT. The head row of the HEADLESS piska 283 (inside 24:19; six rows) ({SP_(283, 1, "ולא", "הגדיש")} "and not the stack"; {SP_(283, 1, "שני", "עמרים", "שכחה", "שלשה", "אינם", "שכחה")} "two sheaves are forgotten, three are not"; {SP_(283, 1, "שני", "גרגרים", "פרט")} "two berries are fallen grapes"): THE COUNT PARAMETER — two forgotten, three a stack (Peah 6:5 the English\'s "//"); one rule for the sheaf, the olive, the carob and the grape. Fresh.')
srow(283, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE FIELD" — EXCLUDING THE BURIED: R. JUDAH; THE SAGES: "IN THE FIELD" INCLUDES THE BURIED. "IN THE FIELD" — TO INCLUDE STANDING GRAIN: THE A FORTIORI FROM THE SHEAF (WHERE THE POOR MAN\'S POWER IS WEAK) ANSWERED — THE SHEAF SAVES NEITHER SHEAF NOR STANDING GRAIN, THE STANDING GRAIN SAVES BOTH — SO THE VERSE TEACHES IT. ({SP_(283, 2, "פרט", "לטמונים")} "excluding the buried"; {SP_(283, 2, "לרבות", "את", "הטמונים")} "to include the buried"; {SP_(283, 2, "לרבות", "את", "הקמה")} "to include the standing grain"; {SP_(283, 2, "שהורע", "כח", "עני", "בו")} "in which the poor man\'s power is weak"): Peah 6:10 and 6:8 — the forgotten standing grain a parameter the argument cannot reach and the word supplies. Fresh.')
srow(283, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"RETURN NOT TO TAKE IT" — EXCLUDING THE HEADS OF ROWS; HENCE: THE HEADS OF ROWS — THE SHEAF OPPOSITE PROVES IT; THE SHEAF HE TOOK HOLD OF TO CARRY TO THE CITY AND FORGOT — THEY AGREE IT IS NOT FORGOTTEN. ({SP_(283, 3, "פרט", "לראשי", "שורות")} "excluding the heads of rows"; {SP_(283, 3, "שהחזיק", "בו", "להוליכו", "לעיר", "ושכחו")} "which he took hold of to carry to the city and forgot"; {SP_(283, 3, "מודים", "שאין", "שכחה")} "they agree it is not forgotten"): Peah 6:2-3 — the return\'s bar on what was never forgotten in the field\'s sense; the two schools agreeing. Fresh.')
srow(283, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"RETURN NOT TO TAKE IT" — ALL OF IT AT ONCE; HOW MUCH? THE SAGES ESTIMATED TWO SEAHS\' YIELD; HENCE: A SHEAF OF TWO SEAHS FORGOTTEN IS NOT FORGOTTEN; TWO SHEAVES OF TWO SEAHS TOGETHER — RABBAN GAMLIEL: THE OWNER\'S; THE SAGES: THE POOR\'S — ETC., THE MISHNAH. ({SP_(283, 4, "כלו", "כאחד")} "all of it at once"; {SP_(283, 4, "שערו", "חכמים", "בעושה", "סאתים")} "the sages estimated at two seahs\' yield"; {SP_(283, 4, "רבן", "גמליאל", "אומר", "לבעל", "הבית")} "Rabban Gamliel says: the owner\'s"; {SP_(283, 4, "וחכמים", "אומרים", "לעניים")} "and the sages say: the poor\'s"): THE MEASURE PARAMETER two seahs and THE MISHNAH BY ABBREVIATION (Peah 6:6 — the English supplies the dialogue in braces); the sheaf too big to forget. Fresh.')
srow(283, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"RETURN NOT TO TAKE IT" — R. ISHMAEL: AN EAR IN THE HARVEST WHOSE HEAD REACHES THE STANDING GRAIN — IF IT COULD BE REAPED WITH IT, THE OWNER\'S; IF NOT, THE POOR\'S. AN OWNER WHO CLAIMS FROM THE POOR MUST BRING PROOF, FOR HE WHO CLAIMS FROM HIS FELLOW BEARS THE PROOF. DOUBTFUL GLEANING IS GLEANING, DOUBTFUL SHEAF A SHEAF, DOUBTFUL CORNER A CORNER — "FOR THE SOJOURNER … LET IT BE". ({SP_(283, 5, "שבלת", "שבקציר", "וראשה", "מגיע", "לקמה")} "an ear in the harvest whose head reaches the standing grain"; {SP_(283, 5, "שהמוציא", "מחברו", "עליו", "הראיה")} "he who claims from his fellow bears the proof"; {SP_(283, 5, "שספק", "לקט", "לקט")} "doubtful gleaning is gleaning"): Peah 5:2 and Eduyot 2:4 (the English\'s "=") — THE BURDEN OF PROOF named as a general rule in the spine, and THE DOUBT RESOLVED FOR THE POOR: two court parameters from one verse. Fresh.')
srow(283, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'R. ELAZAR B. AZARIAH: ONE WHO LOSES A SELA FROM HIS HAND, AND A POOR MAN FINDS IT AND LIVES ON IT — SCRIPTURE COUNTS HIM AS IF HE MERITED; AN A FORTIORI FOR ONE WHO MEANS IT. ({SP_(283, 6, "למאבד", "סלע", "מתוך", "ידו")} "one who loses a sela from his hand"; {SP_(283, 6, "ומצאה", "עני")} "and a poor man found it"; {SP_(283, 6, "כאלו", "זכה")} "as if he merited"; {SP_(283, 6, "קל", "וחמר")} "an a fortiori argument"): 252:2\'s argument on the unmeant good — the forgotten sheaf its Torah seat; the headless piska\'s last row. Fresh.')
srow(284, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU BEAT YOUR OLIVE TREE" (24:20) — THE EARLY ONES BEAT THEIR OLIVES AND DEALT WITH A GENEROUS EYE; HENCE: AN OLIVE TREE STANDING ON THREE ROWS OF TWO BEDS, FORGOTTEN — NOT FORGOTTEN. The head row of piska 284 ({SP_(284, 1, "הראשונים", "היו", "חובטים", "זיתיהם")} "the early ones beat their olives"; {SP_(284, 1, "עין", "יפה")} "a generous eye"; {SP_(284, 1, "על", "שלש", "שורות", "של", "שני", "מלבנים")} "on three rows of two beds"; {SP_(284, 1, "אינו", "שכחה")} "is not forgotten"): Peah 7:2 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=", its continuation supplied in braces — the Netofah olive) — the tree too marked to forget, the sheaf\'s rule on the orchard. Fresh.')
srow(284, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR OLIVES" — EXCLUDING OTHERS\'; EXCLUDING THE CONSECRATED. ({SP_(284, 2, "פרט", "לאחרים")} "excluding others"; {SP_(284, 2, "פרט", "להקדש")} "excluding the consecrated"): 282:2\'s two exclusions on the olive. Fresh.')
srow(284, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"GO NOT OVER THE BOUGHS" — GLORY NOT OVER THE POOR WITH IT; HENCE: HE WHO LETS NOT THE POOR GLEAN, OR LETS ONE AND NOT ANOTHER, OR HELPS ONE OF THEM — ROBS THE POOR; PROVERBS 22:28 "REMOVE NOT THE ANCIENT BOUNDARY". ({SP_(284, 3, "לא", "תתפאר", "לעני", "בו")} "glory not over the poor with it"; {SP_(284, 3, "שאינו", "מניח", "את", "העניים", "ללקט")} "who lets not the poor glean"; {SP_(284, 3, "הרי", "זה", "גוזל", "את", "העניים")} "he robs the poor"): Peah 5:6 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — the rare verb read by its other sense (glory), the owner\'s interference a robbery; the Writings\' verse the seal. Fresh.')
srow(284, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AFTER YOU" — IT HAS A FORGETTING. ({SP_(284, 4, "שיש", "לו", "שכחה")} "it has a forgetting"): the olive under the sheaf\'s law. Fresh.')
srow(284, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AFTER YOU" — IT HAS A CORNER. ({SP_(284, 5, "שיש", "לו", "פאה")} "it has a corner"): the olive under the corner\'s law (Leviticus 19:9). Fresh.')
srow(284, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE SOJOURNER, THE ORPHAN AND THE WIDOW" — "SOJOURNER AND ORPHAN" SAID HERE AND SAID THERE (24:19): AS THERE AT TWO SEAHS\' YIELD, SO HERE AT TWO SEAHS\' YIELD. ({SP_(284, 6, "נאמר", "כאן", "גר", "ויתום", "ונאמר", "להלן", "גר", "ויתום")} "\'sojourner and orphan\' is said here and said there"; {SP_(284, 6, "בעושה", "סאתים")} "at two seahs\' yield"): THE VERBAL ANALOGY CARRYING THE MEASURE from the sheaf to the olive — 283:4\'s parameter reused by the shared words. Fresh.')
srow(285, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU GATHER YOUR VINEYARD" (24:21) — R. ELIEZER: A VINEYARD ALL SMALL CLUSTERS IS THE OWNER\'S; R. AKIVA: THE POOR\'S. The head row of piska 285 ({SP_(285, 1, "כרם", "שכלו", "עוללות")} "a vineyard all small clusters"; {SP_(285, 1, "לבעל", "הבית")} "the owner\'s"; {SP_(285, 1, "לעניים")} "the poor\'s"): Peah 7:7 — the edge case of a whole vineyard of the poor\'s share, disputed. Fresh.')
srow(285, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"GLEAN NOT THE SMALL CLUSTERS" — WHAT IS A SMALL CLUSTER? ONE WITH NEITHER SHOULDER NOR PENDANT; A SHOULDER WITHOUT PENDANT OR A PENDANT WITHOUT SHOULDER — THE OWNER\'S; NEITHER — THE POOR\'S. ({SP_(285, 2, "איזו", "היא", "עוללת")} "what is a small cluster?"; {SP_(285, 2, "לא", "כתף", "ולא", "נטף")} "neither shoulder nor pendant"): Peah 7:4 — the cluster\'s two shapes the definition; the rare verb (olel) kept by Onkelos (24:21\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(285, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AFTER YOU" — IT HAS A FORGETTING; "AFTER YOU" — IT HAS A CORNER; HENCE: WHAT IS FORGETTING ON A TRELLIS? ANY CLUSTER HE CANNOT STRETCH HIS HAND AND TAKE; IN TRAILING VINES — ONCE HE PASSES IT. ({SP_(285, 3, "איזו", "היא", "שכחה", "בעריס")} "what is forgetting on a trellis?"; {SP_(285, 3, "לפשט", "את", "ידו", "ולטלה")} "to stretch his hand and take it"; {SP_(285, 3, "ברגליות", "משיעבר", "הימנה")} "in trailing vines, once he passes it"): Peah 7:8 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — forgetting defined by reach and by passing, two parameters by the vine\'s training. Fresh.')
srow(285, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"SOJOURNER, ORPHAN" — SAID HERE AND SAID THERE (24:19): AS THERE AT TWO SEAHS\' YIELD, SO HERE. ({SP_(285, 4, "נאמר", "כאן", "גר", "ויתום")} "\'sojourner and orphan\' is said here"; {SP_(285, 4, "בעושה", "סאתים")} "at two seahs\' yield"): 284:6\'s analogy for the vineyard — the chapter\'s last row; 286:1 opens on 25:1 (the edge clean, the ink\'s assert). Fresh.')
